--TEST--
No `catch` arm admits the ending `Core\Script::finish()` raises, and the exit report names it `Finish` with status `0` and no error — `rule:observability/three-endings-fire-the-exit-queue`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The other half of the mechanism. The value raised is a root of its own in the
// exception tree — it descends from `Throwable` and from nothing else does
// either — so the self-or-ancestor walk every arm is selected by is false for
// all of them, including the widest one a program can write. An implementation
// that made the marker a `Throwable` subclass would print `caught` here and
// hand a request's cleanup handler an ending it has no business seeing.
// covers: Core\Script\ExitReason
Core\Script::onExit(fn (Core\Script\ExitReport $report): void => {
    string $reason = match ($report->reason()) {
        Core\Script\ExitReason::Normal => "Normal",
        Core\Script\ExitReason::ExitCall => "ExitCall",
        Core\Script\ExitReason::UncaughtThrow => "UncaughtThrow",
        Core\Script\ExitReason::Finish => "Finish",
    };
    // Status `0` and no error, asserted together: a finished script has not
    // failed, and the `UncaughtThrow` reading of the same arrival would report
    // `1` and carry the marker as the report's own `error`.
    echo "onExit: ", $reason, " ", $report->status(), " ",
        $report->error() == null ? "no error" : "an error", "\n";
});

try {
    Core\Script::finish();
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    echo "caught by Throwable\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $runtime) {
    echo "caught by RuntimeError\n";
} finally {
    // The `finally` of the very region whose arms all declined it. Both are
    // asserted at once here: declining the value is not declining the region.
    echo "finally of the region that caught nothing\n";
}
echo "this line never runs\n";
--EXPECT--
finally of the region that caught nothing
onExit: Finish 0 no error
